# Caches survive reboot

**Caches must survive app reboot / process death.**

- Prefer **Room** (or equivalent disk) alongside an in-memory layer.
- Session-only / memory-only caches are the exception — only when explicitly justified (e.g. truly ephemeral UI state).
- When adding a new cache: define TTL, hydrate memory from disk on miss, persist after fetch, clear both layers in `clearCache()`.
- Negative results (empty coverage) must be persisted too when they prevent repeated network calls.
